Subject: [PATCH] Widen the pymongo ceiling to the 3.x series

Upstream caps pymongo at <=3.11.4. conda-forge builds pymongo 3.x per Python
and 3.11.4 stops at Python 3.9, so with python_min at 3.11 nothing in that
range is installable and the package cannot be built at all.

pymongo 3.13.0 is the last 3.x release and does resolve on 3.11. djongo
imports and runs against it. The cap is widened to the 3.x boundary rather
than removed, since djongo 1.3 uses pymongo 3 APIs that 4.x dropped.

Without this, pip check reports:

  djongo 1.3.7 has requirement pymongo<=3.11.4,>=3.7.0, but you have pymongo 3.13.0

--- a/pyproject.toml	2026-10-03 22:22:55
+++ b/pyproject.toml	2026-10-03 22:22:55
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 name = "djongo"
 dependencies = [
     'sqlparse==0.2.4',
-    'pymongo>=3.7.0,<=3.11.4',
+    'pymongo>=3.7.0,<4',
     'django>=2.1,<=3.1.12',
     'pytz>=2018.5'
 ]
